Hi! Sorry for the slow reply.

In this case, if you change

max_range_size = 1

to

max_range_size = 2

...it works. If max_range_size = 1, then the standard DEC model can't function on your data, because DEC only allows range-expansion and range-contraction events.  To get from N to P, there has to be an intermediate state of NP, but you've disallowed ranges of size=2 areas, so your data is impossible, so it fails with that warning.

If you actually intended to run some other model, e.g. a standard "Mk" model for a discrete character, that can be done, but it takes a bit of extra work in the script, I have it on phylowiki somewhere & can help if needed.

Cheers,
Nick

